      "Core fitted 1X2/O-U2.5/O-U3.5 calibration exists and is now surfaced via fusion output's `core_calibration` field (1.4.0); it is NOT the same artifact as fusion-level recommendation confidence, which remains blocked until an approved fusion-level calibration exists.",
      "1.4.0 wraps two confirmed core-engine crash scenarios (ZeroDivisionError / TypeError on stale-anchor inputs) into structured `fusion_status=blocked` responses instead of raw tracebacks; see references/pitfalls.md 1.1. Root cause not yet fixed in core predict.py.",
